		{
			dependencies: ["7E64EF50D212B5C5"]
			description: [
				"Revered as a holy artifact from ancient times, the &aEvil Eye&r is no simple trinket-it is a powerful talisman said to shield its bearer from misfortune and turn aside dark intentions.  "
				""
				"The pieces required to complete the Evil Eye are bound to civilizations that once sought divine protection against the darkness.  "
				"The following pages will guide you on your sacred journey."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"- &lAncient Vases (Green and Blue)&r:  "
				"  Preserved treasures of forgotten civilizations, these vases carry the whispers of prayers and rituals from a lost age.  "
				"  They can be found hidden within the &eCatacombs&r of &eBetter Archeology&r, or obtained through careful trade with Villagers.  "
				"{image:ftb:textures/catacombs.png width:150 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"- &lVillager Hat&r:  "
				"  A relic buried within timeworn settlements, often discovered in &eTrail Ruins&r through careful sifting of suspicious sand and gravel.  "
				"  They can also sometimes be found among the relics scattered through &eIntegrated Villages&r.  "
				"{image:ftb:textures/trail_ruins.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"- &lVillager Fossil Skull&r:  "
				"  The sacred remains of ancient villagers, fossilized and hidden within &eFossiliferous Dirt&r found deep within the &eVillager Graves&r of &eBetter Archeology&r.  "
				"  These skulls serve as a grim testament to forgotten generations who sought the blessings of the Evil Eye.  "
				"{image:ftb:textures/villager_grave.png width:150 height:100 align:center}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				" &nThe Evil Eye is a gift-but one not granted lightly.&r  "
				"You must honor the ruins of the past, brave the forgotten catacombs, and unearth sacred relics to forge this talisman of protection.  "
				"Only those with pure determination and careful hands can claim the blessing of the ancients and wield the Evil Eye’s warding power."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "endrem:evil_eye"
				tag: {
